From 8000a97dcca925f6b4dc13e3d2783039ed7b3894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Moskowski <me@corpix.ru>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] show the creating network namespace

The kernel reports the namespace where a WireGuard interface was
created as an ID relative to the reader. Read that signed attribute and
look through RUNSTATEDIR/netns with RTM_GETNSID for a matching name, the
same way ip turns a link netns ID back into a name.

Show the name when one is available and keep the numeric ID when the
namespace has no name. A negative ID is shown as unknown, while a kernel
without the attribute leaves the field absent.

Add creating-netns to the script-friendly selectors and to the normal
interface display. Append it to the device row in dump output as well;
showconf is unchanged because the namespace is runtime state, not
configuration.
